  "root_cause_analysis": "The model violated two core playbook rules: (1) delta6 requires returning only tool output tuples with no narrative, and (2) delta10 prohibits retry loops—the model should execute one atomic operation per turn and yield immediately. Instead, it chained exploratory commands (cd/ls/find) and attempted multiple mv paths, exhausting the inference budget.",
  "correct_approach": "Turn 0: Execute only `mkdir {\"dir_name\": \"Projects\"}` and yield. Turn 1: Execute single atomic `mv {\"source\": \"proposal.docx\", \"destination\": \"Projects/final_proposal_2024\"}` (combined rename+move in one call) and yield. Turns 2–5: Execute one atomic operation per turn (touch, echo with redirection, diff, wc) with no chaining or exploratory commands.",
  "key_insight": "Multi-turn tasks require strict adherence to atomic execution: one state-mutating operation per turn, immediate yield, no narrative text, and no retry loops. The model's exploratory cd/ls/find chains and narrative commentary consumed the inference budget before reaching the required file operations (touch, echo, diff, wc)."
}

